=== 19:51 PRE-REGISTRATION (CAT) -- does carrying the FULL skill catalogue hurt the 27B on tasks that never use a skill?
Written before any run. Follows ADR-0158 fourth addendum ("the next question for small models is end-to-end"). The extreme
is tested before the middle: if a 146-skill catalogue the model never needs costs nothing end to end, a top-K shortlist
cannot be worth building for outcomes (only for latency/cost), and vice versa.

Cells (zc-01, pod zakpod1, model zds-qwen3.8-27b, temperature 0, ZAKCODE_STABLE_PROMPT_IDENTITY=1, ZBENCH_PIN_MODE=workspace,
ZAKCODE_HOME=/root/zbench-home, request dumps on, N=3 runs per task per arm, determinism_arm.py as the runner):
  NONE  the bench default: no skills root, enable_skills off (no catalogue, no use_skill/save_skill tools)
  FULL  ZBENCH_SKILLS_ROOT=/opt/mind-skills-root (Ayoai-Mind's committed .claude/skills, 146 SKILL.md, rendered catalogue
        83,164 chars ~20k tokens on this Mind) -> enable_skills on: catalogue in the stable tier + use_skill/save_skill tools.
        The arm therefore measures "carrying skills" as a package (catalogue + two tools), not the catalogue text alone.
Tasks: 02-median-bug, 03-lru, 06-plugin-conventions, 07-ttl-cache, 08-mutation-leak (none needs a skill; 27B baselines today:
02 3/3, 03 12/12, 06 3/3, 07 10/18, 08 6/6). 5 tasks x 2 arms x 3 = 30 runs. Order: per task, NONE then FULL.
Positive control (instrument): the FULL arm's dumped system prompt carries the "Available skills" block and is >= 60,000 chars
longer than NONE's for the same task; NONE's carries no such block. Either failing = instrument refusal, not a result.

Predictions (H1: the catalogue crowds the small model):
  P1 pooled pass count over 15 runs/arm: FULL < NONE.
  P2 wall time: FULL median elapsed_s per run > NONE (extra prefill on every cache miss; ADR-0157 showed cache state moves).
  P3 turns: FULL mean num_turns >= NONE; any use_skill call in a FULL run is counted (distraction into skills on a code task).
  P4 byte-identity: unchanged by the arm -- 02/06/08 identical 3/3 in BOTH arms (the catalogue is a static prefix).
Decision rules:
  R1 FULL passes <= NONE passes - 3  -> the catalogue costs OUTCOMES on the 27B; the budget lever is real; build the shortlist.
  R2 |FULL - NONE| <= 2 passes       -> no outcome effect at N=15; the lever is latency/cost only; the shortlist is not built
                                        for outcomes (a smaller catalogue may still be shipped for latency, decided on P2).
  R3 FULL >= NONE + 3                -> surprising; record; no claim without replication.
  R4 P2 ratio (FULL/NONE median elapsed) > 1.25 -> latency cost is material and reported as such; <= 1.25 -> not material.
  R5 P4 broken in FULL only (identity lost where NONE keeps it) -> the longer static prefix changes the endpoint's numerics;
                                        record beside ADR-0157; no product change.
  R6 any FULL run that calls use_skill -> counted and named; if >= 3 of 15 runs wander into skills, that mechanism is reported
                                        as the cost even when R2 holds.
Not claimed by any outcome: anything about the 35B, the coach's 58-skill catalogue, or tasks that DO need a skill (none exists
in the bench yet). Results are appended below, stamped with the box clock.

