Positive control HOLDS: main-loop system prompt 93,207 vs 9,827 chars (delta +83,380), skills block only in FULL, 27 vs 25 tools.
Predictions: P1 FAILED (pooled passes equal); P2 HELD (median 1.38x, slower on 4 of 5 tasks); P3 HELD (mean turns 16.2 vs 12.5,
carried by 06 and 07); P4 FAILED on 2 of the 4 tasks NONE reproduced (03 and 06 lost byte-identity under FULL; 02 and 08 kept it).
Rules as written: R2 (FULL - NONE = 0 passes -> no outcome effect at N=15; the lever is latency/cost only; the shortlist is not
built for outcomes). R4 1.38 > 1.25 -> latency cost MATERIAL. R5 identity lost in FULL only on 03-lru and 06-plugin-conventions.
R6 not triggered: 0 use_skill and 0 save_skill calls in 15 FULL runs -- the catalogue acted purely as context.
What the pooled count hides: two 3-to-0 reversals in opposite directions on the two tasks the 27B is marginal on (06 lost, 07 won).
At temperature 0 with pinned prompts the three repeats of a cell are a reproducibility check, not three samples (02/06/08 NONE were
byte-identical), so the effective replication unit is the task: 5 conditions per arm, and each reversal is one re-rolled basin --
the 83,380-char prefix is a prompt change like any other (ADR-0157). The pre-registration counted 15 runs as if independent; this
limitation is recorded, and the pooled R2 verdict is read as "no net effect across five tasks", not as a 15-sample estimate.
06 mechanism (dumps): both arms read the same four files and never CONTRIBUTING.md; from identical evidence the model mirrored the
siblings' stdlib convention 3/3 without the catalogue and imported pyyaml 3/3 with it. 07: under FULL the model roughly doubled its
turns (30-33), added a conftest and more tests, and passed with three different programs; without it, 13-16 turns, the two failing
linked-list designs from the C cells. Same-trajectory latency (identical turns, 02 and 08): FULL 1.4-3.0x slower per run with the
prefix cache warm from run 2 on -- the cost of attending over ~23k extra tokens per step on the 27B, not of extra work.
Decision recorded as ADR-0160.
